        "<b>Body mechanics</b>: wide base, load close, hip hinge, pivot feet, raise the bed. Manual lifting limit about 35 lb (NIOSH).",
        "<b>Safe patient handling</b>: mechanical lifts and friction-reducing devices replace manual lifting of heavy loads.",
        "<b>Guarding</b>: gait belt, stand behind and toward the weaker side; on stairs, stay below the patient.",
        "<b>Controlled fall</b>: do not hold the patient up; widen stance, guide down, protect the head."
