        ["A patient's chart shows MRSA in a wound. Which precautions should the PT follow?", ["Contact precautions with gown and gloves", "Airborne precautions with an N95 respirator", "Droplet precautions with a surgical mask", "Standard precautions without gown or gloves"], "MRSA spreads by contact with the patient and surfaces, so contact precautions apply."],
        ["Before entering a patient room for a first mobility session, what should the PT do FIRST?", ["Review the chart for orders, precautions, and recent vitals", "Apply the gait belt and help the patient stand", "Ask the nurse to bring a walker to the room", "Lower the bed fully and remove the bed rails"], "Chart review identifies weight-bearing orders, precautions, and red flags before any movement begins."],
        ["Why are gloves donned last when putting on PPE?", ["So the glove cuffs cover the gown's wrists", "Because gloves are the least contaminated item", "So hands remain free while removing the mask", "Because gloves must be fitted before the gown"], "Gloves over the gown cuffs creates a barrier and keeps gloves clean until patient contact."]
