        "<b>High-risk sites</b>: sacrum, coccyx, heels, ischial tuberosities, greater trochanters, occiput.",
        "<b>Repositioning</b>: traditionally every 2 hours; individualize by risk and skin response. Use 30° side-lying; head of bed ≤30° when possible.",
        "<b>Float heels</b>: pillow under calves so heels are off the mattress.",
